WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
What do you remember about Governor Edwin Edwards?

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.020
My parents [Valery and Eola Montgomery] was crazy about him.

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:15.880
He would come and they would talk French to each other because Edwards is a Frenchman, too.

4
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.460
And they would talk a little French.

5
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:22.940
And of course I didn’t understand it so I didn’t know what they was talking about. [laughing] I can remember,

6
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.400
I think Ed was the one who helped us to get water in Mossville--city water.

7
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.180
And different things like that.

8
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.860
And I remember they . . . Daddy had to go on TV for the water.

9
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:43.980
And he was working at Conoco and they said that they needed him to be at the station at a certain time.

10
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.360
He said, “Oh, but I’m at work.”

11
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.160
They said, “Oh man!

12
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.240
We need you to come and say something about this because you helped us to get to this point.”

13
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.960
So he said, “Okay, I’m going to ask my boss man, ‘Can I take off to go?’”

14
00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:00.700
And he was so nervous and he told us, he say . . . I can remember that real good.

15
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.180
He say, “I’m going to have to get me a shot of whiskey to calm my nerves down.

16
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.220
I don’t know how to speak on the TV!

17
00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.600
I never did that before,” and stuff.

18
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.470
They say he did good speaking on the TV, and I think his brother, Wes, went, too.

19
00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.260
So yeah, that was something to be proud of.

20
00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.940
Had to fight a while to get sewage here, and water.

21
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.480
Yeah.

22
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.740
He was helping to do all kind of stuff, you know, whenever they needed.

23
00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.240
They was always coming to talk with him about things.
